{
  "_note": "What a clip needs around it (npc/clip_setup.gd; docs/design_route_npc_behavior.md 'clip-setup'). Only clips that need something are listed: a clip for one person that touches nothing and holds nothing is not here. A clip names things, never geometry. post: the kind of place it is played at; where a person stands on an object is only in the object type's Marker3D post_<kind>[_n] (types/*.tscn), and the clip may appear only in post:<kind> rows of the behaviour table (and in crowd-params posts of that kind). item: {type: a types/held_<name>.tscn, hand: left | right | both (the midpoint of the hands) | back (the neck point)}; how it sits in the hand is the offset of that type's model node. Pushed things (carts, strollers) are ordinary objects with a post, in group pushed: they follow the person's root, not a hand. partner: a second person the clip opens a place for: clip (played in step with this one), at [x, z] metres and yaw degrees in this person's frame (+Z = the way this person faces). Missing things (no type offers the post kind, no such held type, no such partner clip) are the one exception to stopping: the clip shows greyed in scenes/empty_ground with what is missing, and the game never picks it.",
